---
// 🤖 Homepage summary. Normative requirements remain in SPEC.md.
const profiles = [
  {
    level: 'L1', title: 'Base', label: 'The system Samuel uses today',
    benefit: 'Your second brain, skills, role agents and tools live in open files. Run them through an existing AI harness, with your own official subscription or API key.',
    dependency: 'Sync adapters, authentication and tool connections for each supported harness. No dedicated YAIBOS app required.',
    exit: 'Change harness while keeping your business files. Verify tools, permissions and schedules in the destination.',
  },
  {
    level: 'L2', title: 'Cockpit', label: 'Optional execution dashboard',
    benefit: 'Everything in Base, plus a catalog to launch skills, follow progress, handle approvals and read run history. Useful even for one person.',
    dependency: 'A dashboard integrated with its supported harnesses. Launch, tracking and cancellation depend on that integration.',
    exit: 'Keep Base and export run records. You may need a different dashboard when you change harness.',
  },
  {
    level: 'L3', title: 'Team', label: 'Optional shared operations',
    benefit: 'Everything in Cockpit, plus shared context, enforced role permissions, area owners and a team audit trail.',
    dependency: 'Identity, shared storage, file sync and access enforcement. More infrastructure to maintain.',
    exit: 'Export files, history and policies. Configure and verify access enforcement again in the destination.',
  },
];
---

<section id="implementation-profiles" class="py-16 px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8 border-b border-slate-200/80 bg-slate-50/40">
  <div class="max-w-6xl mx-auto">
    <div class="max-w-3xl mb-8">
      <h2 class="text-3xl sm:text-4xl font-bold tracking-tight text-slate-900">One portable base. Optional layers when you need them.</h2>
      <p class="mt-4 text-base sm:text-lg text-slate-600 leading-relaxed">Base is complete on its own. Cockpit and Team describe additional capabilities, with more dependence on the chosen integration.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="grid md:grid-cols-3 gap-6">
      {profiles.map((profile) => (
        <article class="rounded-xl border border-slate-200 bg-white p-6">
          <p class="text-xs font-semibold text-blue-700">{profile.level} · {profile.label}</p>
          <h3 class="mt-2 text-2xl font-bold text-slate-900">{profile.title}</h3>
          <p class="mt-3 text-sm text-slate-700 leading-relaxed">{profile.benefit}</p>
          <h4 class="mt-5 text-sm font-semibold text-slate-900">What it depends on</h4>
          <p class="mt-1 text-sm text-slate-600 leading-relaxed">{profile.dependency}</p>
          <h4 class="mt-4 text-sm font-semibold text-slate-900">If you switch</h4>
          <p class="mt-1 text-sm text-slate-600 leading-relaxed">{profile.exit}</p>
        </article>
      ))}
    </div>
    <p class="mt-6 text-sm text-slate-600">The business files remain portable at every level. Identical interface features across harnesses are not guaranteed. <a class="text-blue-700 font-medium hover:underline" href="/spec#2-conventions-and-implementation-profiles">Read the profile requirements →</a></p>
  </div>
</section>
